    <article class="card doc-content prose">
      <div class="kicker">REST APIs</div>
      <h1>Routing multiple endpoints</h1>
      <p class="lead">Use REST mode when you need more than one path under a shared base URL.</p>

      <h2>Example router</h2>
      <div class="codeblock" style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <header><span>api.basil</span><span class="kbd">router</span></header>
        <pre><code>fn handle(req):
  if req.path == "/v1/ping":
    return { status: 200, body: "pong" }
  if req.path == "/v1/version":
    return { status: 200, body: "1" }
  return { status: 404, body: "not found" }</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 14px;">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> keep routes small and composable. For bigger APIs, consider a dedicated service.
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
